    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes made:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n**Issue 1: Missing APPROVAL_STATUSES export**\n- File: `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`\n- Problem: The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it wasn't being exported.\n- Fix: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`.\n\n**Issue 2: toxicityMetric function signature mismatch**\n- File: `packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`\n- Problem: The `toxicityMetric` function expected `(outputs, bannedTerms)`, but `runEvaluations` always calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`. This caused the references array to be incorrectly interpreted as banned terms.\n- Fix: Updated the signature to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` so it accepts the references parameter but ignores it and uses the default banned terms.\n\n**Test Results:** All 28 tests across 8 test files now pass \u2713\n\n**Public Exports:** All existing public exports from `finetune/index.js` and `eval/index.js` remain functional and unchanged.",
